%I A118554 #32 Nov 20 2026 16:16:40
%S A118554 0,11,35,56,104,147,204,336,455,731,980,1311,2079,2772,4380,5831,7760,
%T A118554 12236,16275,25647,34104,45347,71435,94976,149600,198891,264420,
%U A118554 416472,553679,872051,1159340,1541271,2427495,3227196,5082804,6757247,8983304
%N A118554 a(n) = 6*a(n-5) - a(n-10) + 98 with a(0)=0, a(1)=11, a(2)=35, a(3)=56, a(4)=104, a(5)=147, a(6)=204, a(7)=336, a(8)=455, a(9)=731.
%C A118554 X values of solutions to the equation X^2 + (X+49)^2 = Y^2.
%C A118554 Consider all Pythagorean triples (X,X+49,Z) ordered by increasing Z; sequence gives X values.
%C A118554 The nonnegative solutions of x^2 + (x+49)^2 = y^2 form exactly five Pell orbits with canonical seeds (x,y) = (0,49), (11,61), (35,91), (56,119), and (104,185). In the notation of the cited Pell-orbit catalog, H(49) = 5 and P(49) = 2: five solution streams are needed to obtain the increasing x-sequence, and two of these streams consist of primitive Pythagorean triples. - _Farhad Banazadeh_, Nov 12 2026
%H A118554 G. C. Greubel, <a href="/A118554/b118554.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..1000</a>
%H A118554 Farhad Banazadeh, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23592032">A Unified Pell-Orbit Theory for the Diophantine Equation x^2+(x+d)^2=y^2: Complete Parametrization, Recurrences, and an OEIS Catalogue</a>, Zenodo (2026), Section 11.4.8.
%H A118554 <a href="/index/Rec#order_11">Index entries for linear recurrences with constant coefficients</a>, signature (1,0,0,0,6,-6,0,0,0,-1,1).
%F A118554 a(n) = a(n-1) +6*a(n-5) -6*a(n-6) -a(n-10) +a(n-11) with a(0)=0, a(1)=11, a(2)=35, a(3)=56, a(4)=104, a(5)=147, a(6)=204, a(7)=336, a(8)=455, a(9)=731, a(10)=980. - _Harvey P. Dale_, Aug 19 2011
%F A118554 G.f.: x*(11+24*x+21*x^2+48*x^3+43*x^4-9*x^5-12*x^6-7*x^7-12*x^8 -9*x^9)/( (1-x)*(1-6*x^5+x^10)). - _Colin Barker_, Apr 09 2012
%e A118554 The five canonical seeds give the triples (0,49,49), (11,60,61), (35,84,91), (56,105,119), and (104,153,185). Applying the Pell transformation (x,y) -> (3*x + 2*y + 49, 4*x + 3*y + 98) gives the next triples (147,196,245), (204,253,325), (336,385,511), (455,504,679), and (731,780,1069), respectively. - _Farhad Banazadeh_, Nov 12 2026
%t A118554 LinearRecurrence[{1,0,0,0,6,-6,0,0,0,-1,1}, {0,11,35,56,104, 147,204,336, 455,731,980},40] (* _Harvey P. Dale_, Aug 19 2011 *)
%o A118554 (PARI) my(x='x+O('x^40)); concat([0], Vec(x*(11+24*x+21*x^2+48*x^3+43*x^4 -9*x^5-12*x^6-7*x^7-12*x^8 -9*x^9)/((1-x)*(1-6*x^5+x^10)))) \\ _G. C. Greubel_, May 07 2018
%o A118554 (Magma) m:=40; R<x>:=PowerSeriesRing(Integers(), m); [0] cat Coefficients(R!(x*(11+24*x+21*x^2+48*x^3+43*x^4-9*x^5-12*x^6 -7*x^7 -12*x^8 -9*x^9)/( (1-x)*(1-6*x^5+x^10)))); // _G. C. Greubel_, May 07 2018
%o A118554 (Python)
%o A118554 def a118554(n):
%o A118554     if n < 0:
%o A118554         raise ValueError("n must be >= 0")
%o A118554     streams = [(0, 49), (11, 61), (35, 91), (56, 119), (104, 185)]
%o A118554     for _ in range(n):
%o A118554         i = min(range(5), key=lambda j: streams[j][0])
%o A118554         x, y = streams[i]
%o A118554         streams[i] = (3*x + 2*y + 49, 4*x + 3*y + 98)
%o A118554     return min(x for x, y in streams)
%o A118554 print([a118554(n) for n in range(37)]) # _Farhad Banazadeh_, Nov 12 2026
%Y A118554 Cf. A118674 (d=31), A129288 (d=41), A118675 (d=47) for related fixed-difference equations and Pell-orbit decompositions.
